  "name": "barrier-generation-futures",
  "description": "Two barriers at px-b with different generations. Barrier gen 2 closes generation 1; barrier gen 3 closes both 1 and 2. A generation-1 marker that is still in flight when the gen-2 barrier fires blocks it (barrier_unproven); the same marker arriving after generation 1 has been closed is dropped with closed_generation instead of being re-routed. That difference is the point: identical marker state has a different future depending on which barrier generation has already fired. The safe table waits out the slowest permitted link before checking generation 2, then checks generation 3 only after generation 2 has closed.",
